<title>SINGAPORE: Singapore January non-oil exports down 3.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Singapore January non-oil exports down 3.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Singapore's non-oil domestic exports fell a nominal 3.1 percent year-on-year in January to Singapore $7.36 billion after falling 0.5 percent in December, the Trade Development Board (TDB) said on Thursday.  </p>
<p>A Reuters poll of 17 financial institutions had predicted a nominal year-on-year fall of 1.0 percent in January.  </p>
<p>In real terms, non-oil exports rose 0.9 percent in January to S$9.51 billion after rising 4.6 pct in December.</p>
<p>Trade in nominal terms, in bln S$ at current prices</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes given in parentheses)</p>
<p>				   January		 December</p>
<p>    Total trade	   30.85  (0.0)	  31.04  (2.8)</p>
<p>    Exports		 15.07 (-1.5)	  15.08  (5.0)</p>
<p>    Domestic exports     8.90 (-1.4)	   8.86  (2.3)</p>
<p>    Oil			1.54  (7.6)	   1.40 (20.2)</p>
<p>    Non-oil		  7.36 (-3.1)	   7.46 (-0.5)</p>
<p>    Re-exports	     6.18 (-1.7)	   6.22  (9.2)</p>
<p>    Imports		 15.78  (1.5)	  15.96  (0.8)</p>
